  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Let \\(f(t)=\\dfrac{t}{1-t},\\) \\(t\\ne1.\\) If \\(y=f(x),\\) then \\(x\\) can be expressed as:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(f\\left(\\dfrac1y\\right)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(-f(y)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(-f(-y)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(f(-y)\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(f(y)\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1967-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "From \\(y=\\frac{x}{1-x}\\) we obtain \\(y-yx=x,\\) so \\[ x=\\frac{y}{1+y}. \\] Since \\(f(-y)=-\\frac{y}{1+y},\\) this is \\(-f(-y).\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Solve \\(y=\\frac{x}{1-x}\\) for \\(x\\)",
        "Compare \\(\\frac{y}{1+y}\\) with \\(f(-y)\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
